  "resultInterpretation": [
    "Native embedded WebKit: body succeeds at UTF16 offset5 and emoji-removed attachment at17 for production/giu/gi. Original attachment and trailing-space attachment both have direct indexOf19, but production offsets/segments and giu exec/matchAll return empty. Their gi controls return exact query at19.",
    "For the two native failing giu controls, exec begins0, returns null and ends0; separate matchAll begins0, yields[] and leaves source RegExp lastIndex0. In successful controls exec advances to matched end14/26/28; matchAll source object remains0 before/after. These are actual captured values, not assumed RegExp behavior.",
    "Adding one trailing ASCII space preserves the native failure even though the literal ends one UTF16 unit before string end. This fixed counterexample is therefore not explained solely by the query ending at EOF. Removing🙂 changes the offset/length and makes this one payload pass; it does not prove a universal emoji rule.",
    "Chrome executes the same served script and the four captured payloads with correct production offsets/segments and both giu/gi first/all matches. Captured pattern/source/flags and exact input shapes match native. This establishes a bounded cross-surface discrepancy without identifying a precise JavaScriptCore revision or unique internal cause.",
    "The Node baseline records v22.22.3/V8 12.4.254.21-node.56 and TypeScript5.9.3 exact probe execution. Its actual four result objects were compared against Chrome and match; Node success remains a separate environment result, not native acceptance.",
    "This pure-string failure occurs without a conversation DOM/Range/Highlight in the probe and extends the earlier9482 missing-offset observation. It does not retroactively determine the cause of every pixel failure or establish current-source installed behavior.",
    "gi is a diagnostic comparison only; dropping Unicode mode is not adopted or shown semantically equivalent for all supported queries. Production matcher remains the pinned original module in this evidence arm; no source repair, formal installation or complete P12 acceptance is claimed."
  ],
